Sure, here you go. (vanilla-sources-2.6.11.8 config file) Note that I=20
have a few modules you might not need, so tweak those parts as needed.=20
In particular, I enabled the legacy tulip driver as well as the de2104x=20
one because I didn't remember which one worked on my machine, and same=20
thing for my Intel EtherExpress Pro/100 (e100 and eepro100, I can never=20
remember which one works until I try both...).

I think basically, the important thing is the system type setting (set=20
to Alcor/XLT) and the next switch that specifies that you have an ev56=20
processor (boolean). Setting system type to generic would also work, but=20
it presumably disables some optimisations, and setting system type to=20
Alcor/XLT without checking the ev56 switch makes kernel that doesn't=20
boot on XL366.

Other than that, I followed the "Configuring your kernel" part of the=20
Gentoo Handbook, so nothing special there.

BTW, kudos to the Gentoo project for the quality of its documentation!

